WEBVTT

00:04:25.928 --> 00:04:31.100
But there were a few executives
that saw him as a trailblazer,

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:32.310
and actually a couple

00:04:32.351 --> 00:04:35.646
that wanted to invite him
into the board to educate them.

00:04:36.188 --> 00:04:37.315
OK?

00:04:38.065 --> 00:04:41.694
So we've got to the first
key point for our leaders

00:04:41.736 --> 00:04:46.949
is to understand that activism
is in the eye of the beholder,

00:04:46.991 --> 00:04:51.370
as Ruchika Tulshyan, an author
and activist, told us:

00:04:51.412 --> 00:04:57.293
“What looks like rebellion to you
is another person’s basic human rights.”

00:04:57.335 --> 00:05:01.922
So the first thing you've got to do
is really become aware